https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L720-L776


# Vulnerability details


## Proof of Concept

Per conversations and informations provided by the sponsors during the audit, this update is supposed to work smoothly with both evm & non-evm chains, however this invariant doesn't hold, this is because whenever there is a need for transfers, the call route is: `InterchainTokenService#executeWith()/executeWithToken() -> InterchainTokenService#_processInterchainTransferPayload() -> _processInterchainTransferPayload#_giveToken() -> TokenHandler#giveToken() -> TokenManager#addFlowIn() -> TokenManager#_addFlow()`.

Now when processing the interchain transfer payload, there is a need to get the destination address https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L720-L776

```solidity

    function _processInterchainTransferPayload(
        bytes32 commandId,
        address expressExecutor,
        string memory sourceChain,
        bytes memory payload
    ) internal {
        bytes32 tokenId;
        bytes memory sourceAddress;
        address destinationAddress;
        uint256 amount;
        bytes memory data;
        {
            bytes memory destinationAddressBytes;
            (, tokenId, sourceAddress, destinationAddressBytes, amount, data) = abi.decode(
                payload,
                (uint256, bytes32, bytes, bytes, uint256, bytes)
            );
            destinationAddress = destinationAddressBytes.toAddress();
        }

..snip
```

Evidently, this is done with the helper function from the [inherited](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L44-L45) `AddressBytes.sol`: https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/axelar-gmp-sdk-solidity/contracts/libs/AddressBytes.sol#L17-L23

```solidity
    function toAddress(bytes memory bytesAddress) internal pure returns (address addr) {
        if (bytesAddress.length != 20) revert InvalidBytesLength(bytesAddress);

        assembly {
            addr := mload(add(bytesAddress, 20))
        }
    }
```

Evidently, there is an enforcal that the addresses length must be `20`, now whereas this holds true for EVM chains, this isn't true for non-EVM chains as the length of the addresses `!=20`, which then causes the execution attempt to always revert [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L737-L738).

## Impact

As hinted under _Proof of concept_, executions are broken for non-evm chains since they'd always revert [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L737-L738) due to the check on the address's length meaning the integration with Sol/Aptos would not work since the addresses are 32 bytes.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

Correctly support these address types as destinations and reroute the getter logic from `AddressBytes#toAddress()`



